    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 civic is making this really loud, high pitched squealing noise whenever i step on the gas to accelerate. i think it might be a belt issue? can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a bad one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a continuous loop that transfers power from the engine's crankshaft to crucial accessories like the alternator, water pump, and power steering pump. Under heavy acceleration, the belt experiences significant tension and friction, which can cause a bad belt to stall, misalign, or slip on its pulleys. This slipping action creates the loud, high-pitched squealing noise you are hearing, so addressing the belt is likely the first step in resolving this issue. Given the age of your 2018 Civic, it makes perfect sense that a worn-out belt is the culprit behind your noise.",
